{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## 10. Process notes, lessons, open items\n\nInterruptions and recoveries: a session rate limit on 2026-09-06 killed five spec agents mid-run; specs were persisted and relaunched without subagents. On 2026-09-07 the rebar MCP server was slow enough that reads moved to the background and a summary call timed out at 300 s; then the MCP OAuth token expired for this session and for a running subagent, which had verified six cite corrections but could not write them. The operator confirmed the local CLI is the authorized path in that state, and the corrections were applied through it; plan review round 5 also runs through the CLI, unbounded and in the background, per the AGENTS.md rule against timing out gate operations.\n\nAgent-quality lessons recorded: (a) reviewers were right every round, and each block was a grounding defect I could have caught with one more grep; the recurring miss was multi-line parenthesized imports invisible to single-line patterns; (b) an acceptance check that cannot fail (\\s in git grep) is worse than none; (c) my \"three-round rule\" was an invented constraint, corrected; (d) the first cite-fix agent died on a rate limit with nothing written, the second on the token expiry; staging work as files before writing let it survive both; (e) two agent reports needed correction for internal count inconsistencies before ticketing (E10 CI-parity counts; E3 loader cites), and one agent's initial verdict on the duplicate-ticket incident wrongly blamed the janitor sweeps before experiment corrected it to the tier-2 harness.\n\nDurable locations: every epic's first comment holds its research record; every story's first comment holds its mechanics; this log and idea 77e3 hold the analysis; session scratch (proposal document, agent reports, overlap and drift analyses, cite-fix staging) is under the job's temporary directory and is not durable, so nothing decision-bearing was left only there.\n\nOpen items at the time of writing: plan review round 5 for helpless-carnelian-megaraptor (revise and re-run until it passes); the remaining 45 stories still need their own plan reviews before claim; bug 1768 must land before any mechanism-deleting story; the reconciler move needs the operator's force-submit when its lock step is the only red item; ADR numbers resolve at landing; the reconcile bridge and duplicate-ticket cleanup (bugs bafc, 00c1) are the parallel debug session's; idea 77e3 awaits promotion."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788839752104644001,"uuid":"0a68a9fc-d84c-47c9-a493-ba3fa30238fe"}